      "body": "Design decision record for #5843 (knowledge-layer extensibility cluster), following the sibling pattern of #5844 / PR #7906. Design only — no code changed.\n\nEvidence base: the #6435 feature matrix (`doc/knowledge-layer-feature-matrix-6435.md`, PR #7887 merged), §5 #5843 findings. The prerequisite that blocked the earlier packet (task 12818) has cleared: #6435 closed completed 2026-11-09 with the matrix on main.\n\nDecisions recorded in `doc/knowledge-layer-extensibility-5843.md`:\n1. **API first — ADOPT** a local, token-authenticated API over the corpus as the first extensibility surface (Joplin/Anytype shape); one contract for plugins, importers, and AI tools/MCP. Tokens are scoped, revocable, expiring capabilities; per-object reach still resolves through #5678's ruled read-authority order.\n2. **Plugins — ADAPT** declarative, capability-scoped registration against that API; Joplin-style plugin-registered import/export modules adopted for the importer line (#6436, #6438). In-process arbitrary-code community plugins (Obsidian shape) rejected for v1 with the door explicitly kept open via the registration/capability model.\n3. **Embeds/transclusion** — references resolved through the reader's read-authority decision at render time, never copies; denied embeds render an existence-only tombstone (the #5837 no-leak floor; #5844's per-object rule).\n4. **Scripting/automation** — automations are API clients under a named, auditable identity (Notion automations/webhooks shape, adapted local-first); no privileged built-in scripting runtime.\n\nEnterprise-only API tier (NotebookLM) and hosted-only sole surface rejected with reasons. Seven implementation invariants recorded. Parent decisions preserved; nothing re-decided.\n\nCloses #5843 on merge.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797249358&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=9967&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcod