      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Adds the decision record for #5839, the content-model cluster of the #5678 knowledge-layer programme, grounded in the #6435 feature matrix and on #2048's settled note model.\n- Decisions: the note is the only unit of identity (ADAPT — Notion's identity shape, Logseq's structured content); blocks are typed, addressable content inside a note via (note, pinned revision, block) anchors that degrade honestly; outlines are an editing mode over the block tree, freeform/canvas rejected for v1; daily notes are ordinary notes and the journal is a projection (ADAPT); databases are saved views over notes and their typed properties, never a second content store (ADAPT — Anytype sets / Obsidian Bases pattern over Notion's substrate).\n- States read-authority compliance with the #5678 ruling (resolution at the note; transclusion and every view inherit it), six invariants, the rejected alternatives (block-as-object, opaque document, journal-as-store, database-as-substrate), and open questions routed to #5678.\n- Implementation follow-on filed as #8218.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** no content-model cluster record on main; #2048 fixed note identity and typed references but not the block/page/daily-note/database shape.\n- **After:** `doc/2026-11-10T20-12-00Z_design_id_content_model/2026-11-10T20-12-00Z_design_id_content_model.md` plus a `doc/README.md` catalog entry.\n- `git diff --cached --check` — pass; documentation-only, code tests not applicable.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** low\n\nDesign record only; no runtime behaviour changes. Anything that would change a #2048 or #5678 decision is recorded as an open question for the parent, not decided here.\n\nCloses #5839\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796933151&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8219&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fd